Data Visualization
The project uses several visualization techniques to understand the distribution of sales and profit, compare product categories, analyze the effect of discounts, and identify relationships between numerical variables.

1. Sales Distribution
Graph Type: Histogram

The Sales Distribution graph shows how the Sales Amount values are distributed across the dataset. The graph divides the sales values into multiple ranges and shows how many records fall within each range.

Shows the frequency of different sales amounts.
Helps identify the range where most sales transactions occur.
Shows whether sales are concentrated around certain values or spread across a wide range.
Helps identify unusually high or low sales values.
Purpose
This graph provides an overall understanding of the distribution and variation of sales amounts in the dataset.

2. Profit by Category
Graph Type: Bar Plot

This graph compares Profit across the different product categories.

Shows the average profit associated with each category.
Allows direct comparison between product categories.
Helps identify which categories perform better in terms of profitability.
Shows that high sales and high profit are not necessarily the same thing.
Purpose
This visualization helps determine which product categories are more profitable.

3. Sales Distribution by Category
Graph Type: Bar Plot

This graph compares Sales across different product categories.

Shows how sales are distributed among different categories.
Allows comparison of sales performance between categories.
Helps identify categories with higher and lower sales.
Provides a category-level view of overall sales performance.
Purpose
This graph helps identify which product categories contribute more to sales.

4. Profit Distribution
Graph Type: Box Plot

The box plot represents the distribution of Profit values in the dataset.

The box plot provides information about:

Median: The middle profit value.
Quartiles: Shows how the profit values are spread across the dataset.
Interquartile Range (IQR): Shows the central 50% of profit values.
Whiskers: Show the general range of the profit values.
Outliers: Shows profit values that are unusually high or low.
Purpose
This graph helps understand the spread, central tendency, and unusual values in profit.

Unlike the bar chart, which compares categories, the box plot focuses on the overall distribution of profit.

5. Impact of Discount on Profit
Graph Type: Scatter Plot

This scatter plot compares Discount (%) with Profit. The dataset contains discount values of 0%, 5%, 10%, 15%, and 20%.

Each point represents a data record.
The X-axis represents the Discount percentage.
The Y-axis represents Profit.
It shows how profit values vary at different discount levels.
The pattern of the points can be used to observe whether higher discounts are associated with changes in profit.
Purpose
This visualization helps analyze the relationship between discount levels and profit and provides insight into whether discounting may affect profitability.

6. Correlation Heatmap
Graph Type: Correlation Heatmap

The correlation analysis considers numerical variables such as Quantity, Unit Price, Discount, Sales Amount, Cost Price, Profit, Stock Left, Reorder Quantity, Sales, and Delivery Days.

The heatmap shows the strength and direction of relationships between numerical variables.

Some important relationships found in the dataset include:

Sales Amount and Cost Price: Strong positive relationship.
Sales Amount and Profit: Strong positive relationship.
Quantity and Sales Amount: Positive relationship.
Unit Price and Sales Amount: Positive relationship.
Discount and Profit: Weak negative relationship.
Delivery Days and Sales: Almost no relationship.
For example, the correlation between Sales Amount and Cost Price is 0.983984, while the correlation between Sales Amount and Profit is 0.867967.

Purpose
The heatmap helps identify which numerical variables are strongly or weakly related and provides a quick overview of the relationships present in the dataset.

Overall Summary
Visualization	What it explains
Sales Distribution	How Sales Amount values are distributed
Profit by Category	How profitability differs between categories
Sales Distribution by Category	How sales differ between categories
Profit Distribution (Box Plot)	Spread, median, quartiles, and outliers in profit
Impact of Discount on Profit (Scatter Plot)	Relationship between discount percentage and profit
Correlation Heatmap	Strength and direction of relationships between numerical variables
Together, these visualizations provide a detailed view of the dataset by analyzing sales distribution, category performance, profit distribution, discount impact, and relationships between business variables.

